<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:11:32Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Live: Russian attacks target Kyiv bridges, knock out heating and water</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:77e6fa1b62e786ba7c9d5d8a03e8226f00f4ea92c26ce7c198026551ae48dedb</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:10:46Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T01:38:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261117-live-russian-attacks-target-bridges-in-kyiv-knocking-out-heating-and-water-ukraine--ed14a50b56b5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261117-live-russian-attacks-target-bridges-in-kyiv-knocking-out-heating-and-water-ukraine" /><summary type="html">Russian strikes hit two major bridges in Kyiv late Monday, part of an overnight attack that damaged critical infrastructure and disrupted heating and water in parts of the capital, its mayor said. Ukraine's President Volodymyr Zelensky had warned of an attack by Russia even as negotiators representing Kyiv, Europe and the United States held talks on future negotiations with Russia aimed at finding a path to end the war. Follow our liveblog for all the latest.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Russian strikes hit two key bridges in Kyiv, disrupting water and power supplies</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:985ebb6075eec7851a9a48da4927a94e9892d3c57a627c7b2fed34ad99752c2d</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:10:49Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T00:58:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261117-russian-strikes-hit-two-key-bridges-in-kyiv-disrupting-water-and-power-supplies-ukraine--88719774137a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261117-russian-strikes-hit-two-key-bridges-in-kyiv-disrupting-water-and-power-supplies-ukraine" /><summary type="html">Russian forces struck two major bridges crossing the Dnipro River in Kyiv late Monday, damaging critical infrastructure and causing water and power cuts in parts of the Ukrainian capital, Mayor Vitali Klitschko said. The attacks came as Moscow launched a wider wave of drone and missile strikes across Ukraine, including in the regions of Cherkasy and Kharkiv.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Europe hunts for Palantir alternatives as militaries seek to limit US dependence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:555e577b43786f8689cc3fa8033b7615924d45e6c8b19f65a67c0df7569bb5e0</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:11:01Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T22:07:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261116-europe-hunts-for-palantir-alternatives-as-militaries-seek-to-limit-us-dependence--d261bbeac259.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261116-europe-hunts-for-palantir-alternatives-as-militaries-seek-to-limit-us-dependence" /><summary type="html">As Europe's ​defence ministries look to limit dependency on American technology and major software company Palantir Technologies for critical military functions, a growing number of firms within the region are competing for their business. FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney speaks with Arthur Holland Michel, journalist and researcher specialising in emerging military technologies.</summary><category term="A propos" /></entry><entry><title>Europe hunts for Palantir alternatives as militaries seek to limit US dependence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0d89013418bf1ee4a9300af0059be137e92147859ae6a960fbfc686f1a005999</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:11:05Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T22:05:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe-hunts-for-palantir-alternatives-as-militaries-seek-to-limit-us-dependence--784c998c6cef.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe-hunts-for-palantir-alternatives-as-militaries-seek-to-limit-us-dependence" /><summary type="html">As Europe's ​defence ministries look to limit dependency on American technology and major software company Palantir Technologies for critical military functions, a growing number of firms within the region are competing for their business. FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney speaks with Arthur Holland Michel, journalist and researcher specialising in emerging military technologies.</summary></entry><entry><title>Should Ukraine trade Donbas for NATO membership?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bbd5ad8c81acaea0918544bcb23a5f95482bc76d283acf9faed8f95d93d22c03</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:11:28Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T20:27:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261116-should-ukraine-trade-donbas-for-nato-membership--a0b9c11071ee.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261116-should-ukraine-trade-donbas-for-nato-membership" /><summary type="html">President Volodymyr Zelensky asserting that the United States has asked him about a straight-up swap Russia gets the Donbas, the rest of Ukraine gets NATO membership, a guarantee against Moscow later having a second go and annexing the entire country. Whether or not the offer’s real, serious or that either side would accept it. We’ll ask if the talk of partition signals some kind of turning point in a nearly five-year war that's also a brutal stalemate.</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>EU nations unveil Rwanda deal for migrant return hub</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1650539552fb948b3eb5f6184da024144de176feb5fe3470afb1e19d0405e664</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:11:32Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T20:01:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/eu-nations-unveil-rwanda-deal-for-migrant-return-hub--38d2912ee018.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/eu-nations-unveil-rwanda-deal-for-migrant-return-hub" /><summary type="html">Five EU countries including Germany and Denmark on Monday unveiled a deal to establish a migrant deportation centre in Rwanda -- the first such facility outside the bloc. The group, also comprising Austria, Greece and the Netherlands, has been gunning to open a "return-hub" despite rights groups' concerns, after the European Union cleared the way with a recent toughening of migration rules. FRANCE 24's Dave Keating reports from Brussels.</summary></entry><entry><title>Czech mass protests: Media is the first casualty 'when you want to attack democracy'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2bd889d104bdbc18cb3d8941530d6921ce5f1d9a5a1c6a9bbcca2d019ac9e77d</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T18:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/czech-mass-protests-media-is-the-first-casualty-when-you-want-to-attack-democracy--d702c00cffa6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/czech-mass-protests-media-is-the-first-casualty-when-you-want-to-attack-democracy" /><summary type="html">As hundreds of thousands of people gather in Prague to protest the Czech government's proposal to replace public broadcasting licence fees with direct state funding, Delano D'Souza is pleased to welcome Bára Stárek, Executive Director of Díky, že můžem. Stárek warns that the proposed changes offer "no real safeguards" against political influence, pointing to developments in Slovakia and Hungary. She also drew a parallel with the Velvet Revolution of 1989, recalling that "we didn't have a free media and we only had a state media" under communist rule. "Media is the first (line of) attack when you want to attack democracy," she said. With the legislation expected to reach Parliament in January, Stárek believes the demonstrations will continue if the government refuses to engage in any discussions.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia's war on Ukraine: 'Americans want to have a deal whatever the cost for both Ukraine &amp; Europe'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:49913253fd620d6d51dc71eec735be7563f3216a9c4a529025377d2625639e11</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T16:22:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/russia-s-war-on-ukraine-americans-want-to-have-a-deal-whatever-the-cost-for-both-ukraine-europe--19378cdc5fe6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/russia-s-war-on-ukraine-americans-want-to-have-a-deal-whatever-the-cost-for-both-ukraine-europe" /><summary type="html">Delano D'Souza is pleased to welcome Grégoire Roos, Director of the Europe and Russia and Eurasia Programmes at Chatham House. As European countries prepare to take part in the next round of Ukraine peace talks, Roos questions whether having five European representatives could weaken their negotiating position. "The other option is to realize that it dilutes the negotiating power of Europe. And I would lean towards that," he says, proposing Finnish President Alexander Stubb as a possible representative. Roos also points to differences between Washington and European governments over negotiations with Russia. While "the Americans do absolutely want to have a deal whatever the cost for both Ukraine and Europe," he argues that European governments have little choice but to maintain pressure on Moscow, which has yet to abandon its "maximalist demands."</summary></entry><entry><title>New talks held between Kyiv, Europe and the US, Zelensky says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a523d049557a555b830143c84e7044979557e73303a4524e59adcf2cb0b039d9</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T06:52:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261116-live-600-ukrainian-drones-target-moscow-strike-crimea-bridge-halts-traffic--59995b76c236.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261116-live-600-ukrainian-drones-target-moscow-strike-crimea-bridge-halts-traffic" /><summary type="html">European negotiators joined Ukrainian and US envoys online for the first time to strategise ending the Ukraine war, Ukrainian President Zelensky said Monday. This came after US President Donald Trump announced a plan to discuss the conflict during trilateral nuclear talks with Russia and China on the sidelines of the APEC summit in Shenzhen, China Thursday. Read our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Hundreds of thousands of Czechs protest in Prague over public media funding plan</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b1cdefb7ec5da85987a8af33c6fe2d9536abd31327364394e5d8e211b5cf44a2</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T02:28:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261116-czechs-protest-prague-public-media-funding-plan--ea96c7d8c96e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261116-czechs-protest-prague-public-media-funding-plan" /><summary type="html">Hundreds of thousands of Czechs rallied in Prague on Sunday against government plans to replace public media fees with direct state funding, which critics say threatens broadcasters’ independence. Organisers said turnout exceeded a March protest of more than 200,000, potentially making it the largest demonstration since the 1989 Velvet Revolution.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Nearly 2,200 migrants reach Spain's Canary Islands in two days</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9c212ff4a93eefa46fae3679bad426bf00a05206c6a0e84bdeaf646648baad4b</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T21:06:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261115-nearly-2200-migrants-reach-spain-canary-islands-in-two-days--5944f32f14b8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261115-nearly-2200-migrants-reach-spain-canary-islands-in-two-days" /><summary type="html">Nearly 2,200 migrants have reached the Canary Islands over the past two days, Spain’s coastguard said Sunday, continuing a recent surge of arrivals from West African countries to the Spanish archipelago, where the authorities declared a migration emergency earlier this week.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Prague's fight for public TV: Why a high-profile presenter is prepared to walk away</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1bcd20a4e33caf0e3352e3951d8f5d712eba90058f293a7eb754d21bc492432e</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T19:13:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261115-pragues-s-fight-for-public-tv-why-renowned-presenter-will-leave-czech-tv-over-reforms--1767661cd6ab.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261115-pragues-s-fight-for-public-tv-why-renowned-presenter-will-leave-czech-tv-over-reforms" /><summary type="html">Daniel Stach, one of the Czech Republic’s best-known television presenters and science journalists, tells Gavin Lee on France 24 why he is prepared to walk away from his career rather than work under changes he believes threaten the independence of public broadcasting.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Estonia to close Russian border crossings after 'sabotage' attempt at drone factory</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:acf2482aa2b6a58af23926e580848e7f74162dfedb6b9c8b72591d186737c039</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T17:05:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261115-estonia-to-close-russian-border-crossings-after-sabotage-attempt-at-drone-factory--c99dd3720425.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261115-estonia-to-close-russian-border-crossings-after-sabotage-attempt-at-drone-factory" /><summary type="html">Estonia will close all its border crossing points with Russia from December 1, its ​foreign minister ‌said on Sunday, following a suspected ⁠sabotage attack on an Estonian defence company that Tallinn blamed on ‌Moscow. The Kremlin denied the accusations, calling them "entirely baseless".</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>How did over 2,000 migrants reach the Canaries in just 48 hours?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e96605b09139dc661eaf82926f88317314e6dbc063b64088d0aa07c1a06dd22b</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T16:58:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/how-did-over-2-000-migrants-reach-the-canaries-in-just-48-hours--2665ca66ea37.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/how-did-over-2-000-migrants-reach-the-canaries-in-just-48-hours" /><summary type="html">Spain says nearly 2,200 migrants have arrived by boat to the Canary Islands this weekend. The strip of the Atlantic Ocean between West Africa and the Canary Islands is one of the world's deadliest migration routes – and the journey is usually made with ill-equipped dinghies and overcrowded boats. Details by FRANCE 24 correspondent in Madrid, Sarah Morris.</summary></entry><entry><title>Canaries urge government action after 2,200 migrants reach the islands in 48h</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0e6c7e329c873bade2d46d43d8fa42c203c597537c208d8807d114f932d53b78</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T15:24:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261115-canaries-urge-government-action-after-2-200-migrants-reach-the-islands-in-48h-1--7c412d3109df.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261115-canaries-urge-government-action-after-2-200-migrants-reach-the-islands-in-48h-1" /><summary type="html">Spain says nearly 2,200 migrants have arrived by boat to the Canary Islands this weekend. The Spanish islands are one of the main entry points into Europe for migrants from Africa. The Spanish Interior Ministry says more than 13,000 arrived there between January and the end of last month. Details and analysis by Andrew Hilliar, FRANCE 24 international affairs editor.</summary></entry><entry><title>Santa school in full swing in London ahead of Christmas celebrations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0c632257b680b8ead50b4ea8b0f03e6c8afd0cbf8fcea8d173a4ca3abe573217</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T14:35:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/santa-school-in-full-swing-in-london-ahead-of-christmas-celebrations--5731bcbd3ec7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/santa-school-in-full-swing-in-london-ahead-of-christmas-celebrations" /><summary type="html">It may still be November but it's beginning to look a lot like Christmas in South London, as many Santa impersonators are heading to school for their festive training. The school, organised by an event company called Ministry of Fun, brings together Santas, elves, and Mrs Clauses to share experiences, practice belly laughs and learn how to bring the magic of Christmas to life. Story by Rachael Griffiths.</summary></entry><entry><title>The week in pictures: Spain protests, Pope Leo's Peru 'homecoming' and Rocky fans in Philly</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:56206169078d67aff772438f77ff319d6bba492598db83e074c4e62703b77fa1</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T13:59:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261115-the-week-in-pictures-spain-protests-pope-leo-peru-homecoming-rocky-fans-philly-rosalia--e99d0a43c1b4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261115-the-week-in-pictures-spain-protests-pope-leo-peru-homecoming-rocky-fans-philly-rosalia" /><summary type="html">FRANCE 24 looks back at some of the week's most striking images, from angry protests over a housing crisis that has dominated Spain's election campaign, to Leo XIV's visit to his adopted homeland Peru and "Rocky" fans marking 50 years since the release of boxing movie classic.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Ukrainian drones strike Russia's petrochemical capital in overnight assault</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:be017e172e73ce20014e7bd424cee190df736d8d71d90dc3a85b9748b84a08e5</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T13:36:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261115-ukrainian-drones-strike-russia-s-petrochemical-capital-in-overnight-assault--7a9e9db839b0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261115-ukrainian-drones-strike-russia-s-petrochemical-capital-in-overnight-assault" /><summary type="html">Russian officials confirmed Sunday that the central industrial city of Nizhnekamsk had endured "prolonged" Ukrainian airstrikes overnight, damaging a residential building and sparking a fire at a major petrochemical complex, injuring three people. Separate overnight strikes on Taganrog city killed an electricity substation engineer, according to the regional governor.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Will Ukraine make territorial concessions for NATO membership?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a6338f20f6805d9413cdb9e0438ff79b91a48b674c45cfb0c7b2b61f2a53b4aa</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T12:14:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/will-ukraine-make-territorial-concessions-for-nato-membership--900152e56ff1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/will-ukraine-make-territorial-concessions-for-nato-membership" /><summary type="html">The United States suggested Ukraine make territorial concessions in exchange for a NATO membership, according to Volodymyr Zelensky. The Ukrainian president also claims that Russia has rejected an energy truce. This week’s US-mediated negotiations did not result in any tangible progress. Story by Simon Moritz.</summary></entry><entry><title>Macron says limiting Ukraine aid would pave way to 'another war'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:66b032ffdbd5bf74d6abd45115b778eb2b8734f35c7d0dbb70ce6a1ae1705d7c</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T20:15:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261114-macron-says-limiting-ukraine-aid-would-pave-way-to-another-war--f4035bbf29fb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261114-macron-says-limiting-ukraine-aid-would-pave-way-to-another-war" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron on Saturday warned that limiting aid to Ukraine would force Kyiv into an "unjust peace" and risk another war. His statement comes as the United States pushes ahead with efforts to negotiate between Ukraine and Moscow.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Who are the 'street medics' showing up at protests around the world?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b7428ac09b6b3ece69877c709661c2ba872e6fd0589d11b2171a2ca5142b0438</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T12:19:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/who-are-the-street-medics-showing-up-at-protests-around-the-world--0c414d784e65.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/who-are-the-street-medics-showing-up-at-protests-around-the-world" /><summary type="html">From treating tear gas exposure to tending to injuries, street medics have become an increasingly common sight at protests all over the world. But who exactly are they and when did they start showing up at demonstrations? Story by Daniel Quinlan.</summary></entry><entry><title>US proposed Ukraine cedes Donbas in exchange for joining NATO, Zelensky says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c8d735e97bd748298d72726d6ceb81ca3b5705da2eac2724c1fe8a0b8f183f32</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T10:30:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261114-us-negotiators-suggest-ukraine-cedes-territory-in-exchange-for-nato-membership--b3597e97289d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261114-us-negotiators-suggest-ukraine-cedes-territory-in-exchange-for-nato-membership" /><summary type="html">President Zelensky said the US had proposed ceding Ukraine's eastern city of Donbas to Russia, in exchange for Ukrainian membership of NATO, following the latest round of peace talks in Abu Dhabi this week. He reiterated that Kyiv was not willing to retreat from its territory and warned that the Kremlin's bid to change the continent's security architecture could lead to more wars.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>France among five major powers to represent EU in Ukraine talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ab96867ed3181a681db25418f7218296861eab8c3ee2a9ca8876fd705759f164</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T21:38:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261113-europe-to-send-diplomats-from-across-the-continent-to-ukraine-peace-talks--44eded81bb78.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261113-europe-to-send-diplomats-from-across-the-continent-to-ukraine-peace-talks" /><summary type="html">European Council President Antonio Costa on Friday said that Brussels will send diplomats from the bloc and five countries, including the UK, France, Germany, Italy and Poland, to upcoming Ukraine talks.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>The Downfall of AI’s ‘Rock Star’ Boss, Ukraine: Who speaks for Europe? Protests &amp; Presidents</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:39b4bf95348693b93255af93aa9f8f6fdd1661be66ed67adefe196bf1f1c8310</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T19:46:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-world-this-week/20261113-the-downfall-of-ai-s-rock-star-boss-ukraine-who-speak-for-europe-protests-presidents--795148188632.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-world-this-week/20261113-the-downfall-of-ai-s-rock-star-boss-ukraine-who-speak-for-europe-protests-presidents" /><summary type="html">On The World This Week with Gavin Lee, our panel distills the breaking news and global stories of the past 7 days into 45 minutes. 
 
Ukraine: Who will speak for Europe?
 
In a week thats seen the first direct talks between Ukraine and Russia since February, with the US in the room and the Europeans relegated to the lobby according to Moscow. A new ‘European Security Architecture’ is discussed.</summary><category term="The World This Week" /></entry><entry><title>Hurry up and wait: Europe wants a place at the table, ‘must make up its mind’ over Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2bd33df30995de758cc7afb79bf44675e27cd9e88de39989923b548d3ee76471</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T19:03:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261113-hurry-up-and-wait-europe-wants-a-place-at-the-table-must-make-up-its-mind-over-ukraine--0ede6861b758.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261113-hurry-up-and-wait-europe-wants-a-place-at-the-table-must-make-up-its-mind-over-ukraine" /><summary type="html">Gavin Lee is pleased to welcome Alexander Titov, Lecturer in Modern European History at Queen's University Belfast and a specialist on Russia. He's joined us to discuss high-level meetings in Abu Dhabi, Dublin and the prospects for ending the war in Ukraine.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>'We have done all our homework' to get EU candidate status: Kosovo's PM Albin Kurti</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:11b1eb367dc48ead1342dc0c66cf8c3cb0bd0a031aebf24124d1a5e6391c1c6c</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T17:46:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261113-we-have-done-all-our-homework-to-get-eu-candidate-status-kosovo-s-pm-albin-kurti--597ebf8d6a3e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261113-we-have-done-all-our-homework-to-get-eu-candidate-status-kosovo-s-pm-albin-kurti" /><summary type="html">FRANCE 24 hosts Albin Kurti, the prime minister of Kosovo, a country that declared its independence from Serbia back in 2008 and sees itself as part of the European family. But four years after applying to join the EU, Kosovo has still not received candidate status. We explore Kosovo's path towards the EU, and the broader European and regional dynamics surrounding that.</summary><category term="Talking Europe" /></entry><entry><title>As EU grapples with fierce AI competition, summit overshadowed by elusive Ukraine-Russia peace deal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aaeca48e09cd43d345ef821dfc1c21a428fd0b47d5c8ae8ce395cfda4647785f</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T17:28:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261113-as-eu-grapples-with-fierce-ai-competition-summit-overshadowed-by-elusive-ukraine-russia-pea--d418c75912c1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261113-as-eu-grapples-with-fierce-ai-competition-summit-overshadowed-by-elusive-ukraine-russia-peace-deal-1" /><summary type="html">As EU leaders meet for an AI summit in Dublin, largely overshadowed by Russia's war on Ukraine, William Hilderbrandt is pleased to welcome Fabrice Pothier, CEO of Rasmussen Global. On AI, Pothier points to Europe's limited computing capacity, estimating that it barely represents "5% of what's available out there." Despite the EU's wealth of researchers and expertise, he warns that Europe is struggling to turn these resources into "real technological and industrial scale." Now, turning to the war in Ukraine, Pothier argues that European governments should focus less on "whether they have a place at the table" and more on "making Ukraine's hands stronger," particularly by providing additional air defence interceptors.</summary></entry><entry><title>November 13 Paris attacks: Eleven years later, France pays tribute to victims</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:daef8c884f5714977a0f94b3950f12738d41a7ea98960e25b57b2d9e0399c08f</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T16:47:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/november-13-paris-attacks-eleven-years-later-france-pays-tribute-to-victims--43a7704539a3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/november-13-paris-attacks-eleven-years-later-france-pays-tribute-to-victims" /><summary type="html">Eleven years on, France pays tribute to the victims of the November 13 attacks. French officials, victims’ associations and families gathered this Friday to pay their respects to those killed in the attacks in Paris on November 13, 2015.</summary></entry><entry><title>West Bank: ‘Without international trade and financial support, large settlements would not exist’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:181c22274ec783ef2acb62c3904b199ee58cd81694da1e6cbced2b4c466e2462</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T16:15:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261113-west-bank-without-international-trade-and-financial-support-large-settlements-would-not-exi--ca01d4fe66ed.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261113-west-bank-without-international-trade-and-financial-support-large-settlements-would-not-exist-1" /><summary type="html">France is considering legislation to restrict trade with Israeli settlements in the occupied Palestinian territories, namely the West Bank. Ivar Ekeland, Professor Emeritus at Paris Dauphine-PSL University and Chair of the Organization of Academics for the Respect of International Law in Palestine, discusses the proposed measures with Alison Sargent. He calls for restrictions to cover n ot only goods but also services, including financial services, insurance and tourism. "Without the support of financial entities, of insurance, of providing goods and so on, settlements, big settlements, would not exist," he argues.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia strikes targets across Ukraine as Kyiv launches nearly 1,200 drones</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4509748e31b422cd32e7d5435fb1c1fb5005e9cbff5044d60ea0355c3d7448e9</id><updated>2026-11-17T08:09:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T15:46:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261113-russian-airstrikes-continue-ukraine-launches-nearly-1-200-drones--8c91678fb217.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261113-russian-airstrikes-continue-ukraine-launches-nearly-1-200-drones" /><summary type="html">Russian strikes hit targets across Ukraine on Thursday, with one attack damaging a hospital. Ukraine meanwhile fired almost 1,200 drones at Russian targets overnight in one of its biggest aerial attacks since Moscow’s full-scale invasion nearly five years ago.</summary></entry></feed>
